title: Union Relations
new-page: true
view-if: CHP_party_leader == "Ecevit" and union_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; union_timer = 0
is-card: true
card-image: img/disk.jpg
tags: party_affairs, disk

= Union Relations

Our party has been the progressive people's party of our republic since its birth after the War of Independence. However, the definition of "people" in our name requires clarification.

According to the party's traditional stance, all citizens are considered equal, with no privileges, and are expected to contribute actively to addressing individual needs. Within this framework, the capitalist and financial classes are also regarded as part of the "people."

In contrast, our rising Center of the Left movement, carried by our collective grouping of Leftist Kemalists, offers a more restrictive definition, excluding "exploiters" from the category of the people. Their perspective includes only those who work by their own labor and do not derive income from exploiting others or from holding political or economic power or privileges.

However, this definition must be substantiated through robust engagement with the labor movement to achieve legitimacy and strength. The principal left-wing syndicate, DİSK, has expressed interest in the party's recent direction. Strategies to further strengthen the relationship with DİSK should be considered.

- @municipalities: We have the opportunity to strengthen DİSK within the municipalities under our administration, despite the influence of the right-wing syndicate TÜRK-İŞ.
- @reform: We may commit to implementing extensive labour reforms upon entering government. However, failure to fulfill these commitments could result in significant negative consequences.
- @funding: We could allocate a portion of our party resources to DİSK, although there is a risk that these resources may be absorbed by syndicate bureaucracy.
- @meeting: We might consider arranging a meeting with the chairman of DİSK, Kemal Türkler, to demonstrate our commitment and intentions.
- @root: We can't take any action right now.
- @easy_discard

@municipalities
choose-if: municipality_control_level == 3 or municipality_control_level == 4
unavailable-subtitle: Our control over the municipalities is not sufficient enough!
on-arrival: {! AnatolianCardActions.commitAdvisor(Q); !} disk_relation += 5; disk_turkis_conflict -= 0.05; AP_relation -= 5; DP_relation -= 5

We have empowered DİSK in our municipalities.

@reform
choose-if: not union_reform == yes
unavailable-subtitle: We have already promised extensive labour reforms. Now is the time to enact them.
on-arrival: {! AnatolianCardActions.commitAdvisor(Q); !} disk_relation += 10; AP_relation -= 5; DP_relation -= 5; union_reform = yes

We have promised extensive labour reforms. We have to keep our promise.

@funding
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.,
on-arrival: {! AnatolianCardActions.commitAdvisor(Q); !} resources -= 1; disk_relation += 5; workers_chp += 3

We have transferred some of our resources to DİSK.

@meeting
choose-if: union_visit_timer <= 0
unavailable-subtitle: We have already visited the DİSK headquarters this year. Simply visiting them again will not improve our relations.
on-arrival: {! AnatolianCardActions.commitAdvisor(Q); !} disk_relation += 2; AP_relation -= 2; union_visit_timer = 12

We have paid a visit to the DİSK headquarters. If we want to improve our relations further, we will have to take solid action.

@root

We can't take any action regarding union relations right now.
